# Text in this repository is LF, everywhere, on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# EDA source files are byte-exact. Later rules win, so these override the line
# above. The Protel ASCII PCB format uses CRLF for most records but also carries
# lone CR characters as separators inside them -- those are structure, not line
# endings, and any end-of-line conversion would corrupt the board file.
*.SchDoc -text
*.PcbDoc -text
